    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "TOM MAHER & COMPANY SCSI RICS IPAV - This is a charming 2/ 3  bed semi detached double fronted EXTENDED, SOUTH-EAST FACING family home built circa 1938 complete with c. 53ft rear garden . The property offers tremendous potential to EXTEND TO THE SIDE or REAR subject to the customary planning consents. The property is eligible for the VACANT HOMES REFURBISHMENT GRANT.  The property has been lovingly cared for over the years and presents a wonderful opportunity to create your own DREAM HOME with style and flair. NO ONWARD CHAIN. Newtown Park is an established, mature cul de sac of homes located off the main road, known for its long-standing sense of community dating back over 80 years, a highly connected residential pocket nestled adjacent to a wide range of services and amenities both social and essential, within a pleasant stroll of the village and short commute to the N81/ N7 and M50. REGISTER YOR INTEREST BY EMAIL."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance hall with stairwell\r\nLounge:\t 3.95m x 3.50m (Former Kitchen) feature tiled fireplace, hardwood flooring\r\n2nd reception room : 2.62m x 3.96m Feature Marble Fireplace with Mahogany surround.\r\nKitchen/     Breakfast room : \t3.25m x 3.85mNeat arrangement of built in units and presses. Hot press.\r\nLobby / utility :  .89 x 3.39m plumbed for the washing machine, tiled floor, door off to the garden\r\nBathroom : \t1.97m x 3.25m Mira Elite electric shower - wc – whb – Fully tiled. \r\nUPSTAIRS\r\nBedroom 1 :  3.43m x 3.99m feature Cast-iron fireplace, original built in wardrobe, T & G wood flooring \t \r\nBedroom 2 :  2.70m x 3.98m  feature Cast-iron fireplace, original built in wardrobe"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Double glazed windows throughout.  \r\nThe property has the benefit mains Oil fired radiator  central heating. (PVC tank)\r\nAll main services are laid on \t\t\r\nThe property has a Trip switch fuse board\r\nWalled and hedged garden to the rear, off street parking\r\nBlock garden shed with concrete roof – outside wc – boiler house\r\nBlock shed with windows \r\nFOLIO : \tDN15007F"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Directions",
        "SortOrder": 5,
        "Content": "As per the Map - www.tommaher.ie"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Viewing Details",
